#: codec/1/175/0xafb40/0
msgid ""
"Alternatively, you could try planting Claymores\n"
"along the routes they walk.\n"
msgstr ""
"或者，可以在他们的巡逻路线上\n"
"埋阔剑地雷。\n"

#: codec/1/175/0xafb40/1
msgid ""
"We need you to stop that nuke, Boss.\n"
msgstr ""
"BOSS，得阻止那枚核弹。\n"

#: codec/1/175/0xafb40/2
msgid ""
"We'll keep you safe, no matter what it takes!\n"
msgstr ""
"我们拼了命也会保护你！\n"

#: codec/1/175/0xafca0/0
msgid ""
"It's going to take more than small arms fire to take\n"
"down a truck.\n"
msgstr ""
"光靠轻武器打不掉\n"
"卡车。\n"

#: codec/1/175/0xafca0/1
msgid ""
"Some kind of rocket's your best bet.\n"
msgstr ""
"最好用火箭筒。\n"

#: codec/1/175/0xafca0/2
msgid ""
"Another tactic to try would be setting off an\n"
"explosion from afar.\n"
msgstr ""
"也可以试试从远处\n"
"引爆。\n"

#: codec/1/175/0xafca0/3
msgid ""
"You could also call in a support strike,\n"
msgstr ""
"还可以呼叫支援打击，\n"

#: codec/1/175/0xafca0/4
msgid ""
"if you can manage to tag them with a marker...\n"
msgstr ""
"只要能先用标记器标上他们……\n"

#: codec/1/175/0xafea0/0
msgid ""
"It'll take more than one missile to sink Mother\n"
"Base, but if we do get hit,\n"
msgstr ""
"一发导弹还不足以让母基地沉没，\n"
"可一旦真被击中，\n"

#: codec/1/175/0xafea0/1
msgid ""
"we'll obviously need time, manpower, and materials\n"
"to repair the damage.\n"
msgstr ""
"修复损伤显然需要\n"
"时间、人力和物资。\n"

#: codec/1/175/0xafea0/2
msgid ""
"Do everything you can to keep Mother Base safe.\n"
msgstr ""
"竭尽全力保住母基地。\n"

#: codec/1/175/0xafea0/3
msgid ""
"And, ah, at the risk of stating the obvious: if a\n"
"missile hits you,\n"
msgstr ""
"还有，虽然是废话：\n"
"要是导弹命中你，\n"

#: codec/1/175/0xafea0/4
msgid ""
"you're toast. So don't get hit.\n"
msgstr ""
"你就完了。所以别被打中。\n"

#: codec/1/176/0xb00d0/0
msgid ""
"You'll be using C4 for demolition.\n"
msgstr ""
"爆破要用C4。\n"

#: codec/1/176/0xb00d0/1
msgid ""
"As you might imagine, it's gonna make a big noise\n"
"when it detonates.\n"
msgstr ""
"可以想象，引爆的时候\n"
"会发出巨大的声响。\n"

#: codec/1/176/0xb00d0/2
msgid ""
"For your own safety, make sure you put plenty of\n"
"distance\n"
msgstr ""
"为了自身安全，务必\n"
"保持足够距离。\n"

#: codec/1/176/0xb00d0/3
msgid ""
"between yourself and the C4 before detonating it.\n"
msgstr ""
"离C4远一点。\n"

#: codec/1/176/0xb0290/0
msgid ""
"Boss, we're not sure where your gear is being\n"
"stored.\n"
msgstr ""
"老大，我们不知你的装备\n"
"存哪。\n"

#: codec/1/176/0xb0350/0
msgid ""
"Amanda and her crew tell me they've managed to\n"
"identify several different categories\n"
msgstr ""
"阿曼达的人告诉我，他们已成功\n"
"识别出几个不同类别。\n"

#: codec/1/176/0xb0350/1
msgid ""
"of mercenaries employed by the CIA.\n"
msgstr ""
"几类雇佣兵。\n"

#: codec/1/176/0xb0350/2
msgid ""
"Give me a rundown. Sounds like info I could use.\n"
msgstr ""
"说说看。听起来有用。\n"

#: codec/1/176/0xb0350/3
msgid ""
"No problem. I'll go through them in order.\n"
msgstr ""
"没问题，我按顺序讲。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0520_000_0
#. timeline 445..1058
#: codec/1/176/0xb0510/0
msgid ""
"The type of enemy you'll be seeing most\n"
msgstr ""
"最常见的敌人类型，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0520_000_0
#. timeline 1058..2368
#: codec/1/176/0xb0510/1
msgid ""
"is the type that patrols and guards a specific\n"
"operational area.\n"
msgstr ""
"是负责巡逻和守卫特定\n"
"作战区域的类型。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0520_000_0
#. timeline 2396..3775
#: codec/1/176/0xb0510/2
msgid ""
"For the sake of convenience, Amanda's crew calls\n"
"the outdoor ones \"patrolmen,\"\n"
msgstr ""
"为方便起见，阿曼达的人把\n"
"室外的称为“巡逻兵”，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0520_000_0
#. timeline 3775..4374
#: codec/1/176/0xb0510/3
msgid ""
"and the indoor ones \"guards.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"室内的叫“守卫”。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0520_000_0
#. timeline 4388..5043
#: codec/1/176/0xb0510/4
msgid ""
"They might look like they're just out for a stroll,\n"
msgstr ""
"他们看似只是在闲逛，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0520_000_0
#. timeline 5043..5907
#: codec/1/176/0xb0510/5
msgid ""
"but don't be fooled - they're sharper than they\n"
"look.\n"
msgstr ""
"但别被骗了，他们比看起来\n"
"敏锐得多。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0520_000_0
#. timeline 5948..6757
#: codec/1/176/0xb0510/6
msgid ""
"All of their senses are finely honed.\n"
msgstr ""
"五感都极为灵敏。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0520_000_0
#. timeline 6812..7592
#: codec/1/176/0xb0510/7
msgid ""
"Normally they'll patrol along fixed routes,\n"
msgstr ""
"通常沿固定路线巡逻，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0520_000_0
#. timeline 7592..8818
#: codec/1/176/0xb0510/8
msgid ""
"but when the alert level is raised they'll assume a\n"
"more efficient alert posture\n"
msgstr ""
"但当警戒等级提升时，他们会采取\n"
"更高效的警戒姿态，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0520_000_0
#. timeline 8818..10156
#: codec/1/176/0xb0510/9
msgid ""
"and focus on defending specific points. That's bad\n"
"for you.\n"
msgstr ""
"并专注于防守特定点位。这对你\n"
"很不利。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0520_000_0
#. timeline 10253..10978
#: codec/1/176/0xb0510/10
msgid ""
"Obviously they can hold their own in combat,\n"
msgstr ""
"他们战斗力自然不弱，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0520_000_0
#. timeline 10978..12051
#: codec/1/176/0xb0510/11
msgid ""
"and with body armor it'll be even harder to take\n"
"them down.\n"
msgstr ""
"而且有了防弹衣，就更难\n"
"干掉他们了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0520_000_0
#. timeline 12106..12692
#: codec/1/176/0xb0510/12
msgid ""
"If they're wearing a bulletproof helmet,\n"
msgstr ""
"要是戴着防弹头盔，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0520_000_0
#. timeline 12705..13876
#: codec/1/176/0xb0510/13
msgid ""
"you can forget about one-shot kills. Just a heads\n"
"up.\n"
msgstr ""
"别想一枪毙命了。就\n"
"提醒你下。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0520_000_0
#. timeline 13945..15116
#: codec/1/176/0xb0510/14
msgid ""
"You'll need to be smart about using camo and pick\n"
"your routes.\n"
msgstr ""
"你必须善用迷彩，并谨慎选择\n"
"行进路线。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0520_000_0
#. timeline 15144..16063
#: codec/1/176/0xb0510/15
msgid ""
"The most important thing is to avoid detection.\n"
msgstr ""
"最重要的是别被发现。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0530_000_0
#. timeline 445..1852
#: codec/1/176/0xb0af0/0
msgid ""
"When the enemy spots you and goes on alert, they\n"
"may call in a backup strike team.\n"
msgstr ""
"敌人发现你并警戒时，他们\n"
"可能呼叫后备突击队。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0530_000_0
#. timeline 1866..3120
#: codec/1/176/0xb0af0/1
msgid ""
"These assault teams are heavily armed, well\n"
"trained, and highly dangerous.\n"
msgstr ""
"这些突击队装备精良、训练有素，\n"
"而且极其危险。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0530_000_0
#. timeline 3134..3873
#: codec/1/176/0xb0af0/2
msgid ""
"Amanda's crew calls them \"commandos.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"阿曼达的人管他们叫“突击兵”。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0530_000_0
#. timeline 3900..5670
#: codec/1/176/0xb0af0/3
msgid ""
"Unlike the patrolmen, these guys will actively,\n"
"relentlessly track and hunt you down - like hounds.\n"
msgstr ""
"与巡逻兵不同，这些家伙会主动、\n"
"无情地追踪猎杀你，像猎犬一样。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0530_000_0
#. timeline 6032..7216
#: codec/1/176/0xb0af0/4
msgid ""
"Hounds to hunt a former FOXHOUND... Bring it on.\n"
msgstr ""
"猎犬来猎前FOXHOUND……放马过来。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0530_000_0
#. timeline 7244..8080
#: codec/1/176/0xb0af0/5
msgid ""
"They won't give up easily even if they lose sight of\n"
"you.\n"
msgstr ""
"即使跟丢了你，他们也不会\n"
"轻易放弃。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0530_000_0
#. timeline 8080..9083
#: codec/1/176/0xb0af0/6
msgid ""
"They'll clear out any likely hiding places they come\n"
"across.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们会搜查沿途遇到的\n"
"任何可能藏身之处。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0530_000_0
#. timeline 9097..10267
#: codec/1/176/0xb0af0/7
msgid ""
"So don't get too comfy in one spot or you might\n"
"get caught again.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以别在一处待太舒服，否则可能\n"
"再次被抓。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0530_000_0
#. timeline 10281..11173
#: codec/1/176/0xb0af0/8
msgid ""
"Keep your eyes fixed on them and what they're\n"
"doing.\n"
msgstr ""
"时刻盯紧他们以及他们\n"
"在做什么。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0530_000_0
#. timeline 11229..12329
#: codec/1/176/0xb0af0/9
msgid ""
"Also, be aware that commando gear includes body\n"
"armor.\n"
msgstr ""
"另外注意，突击队装备包括\n"
"防弹衣。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0530_000_0
#. timeline 12329..13305
#: codec/1/176/0xb0af0/10
msgid ""
"So don't think you can deal with them by going in\n"
"guns blazing.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以别以为你可以靠\n"
"猛冲猛打来对付他们。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0530_000_0
#. timeline 13305..14405
#: codec/1/176/0xb0af0/11
msgid ""
"All I've got to do is find an exposed weak point\n"
"and...\n"
msgstr ""
"我只需找到暴露的弱点\n"
"然后……\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1000/0
msgid ""
"There's one type of commando you really need to\n"
"watch out for,\n"
msgstr ""
"有一种突击队员你特别需要\n"
"小心，\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1000/1
msgid ""
"and that's the kind toting shotguns.\n"
msgstr ""
"就是拿霰弹枪的那种。\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1000/2
msgid ""
"They can take a few hits and still keep charging\n"
"you.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们能挨几枪，却仍继续向你\n"
"冲来。\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1000/3
msgid ""
"And believe me, you don't want them closing in\n"
"between those shotgun blasts.\n"
msgstr ""
"相信我，你绝不想让他们在霰弹枪射击间隙\n"
"逼近你。\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1000/4
msgid ""
"When they start charging, you need to stop them\n"
"immediately.\n"
msgstr ""
"当他们开始冲锋时，你必须立刻\n"
"阻止他们。\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1000/5
msgid ""
"Use something with serious stopping power.\n"
msgstr ""
"用制止力强的武器。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0550_000_0
#. timeline 459..1643
#: codec/1/177/0xb1290/0
msgid ""
"We've also confirmed that some of the enemies\n"
"specialize in ambushes.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们还确认，有些敌人\n"
"专门擅长伏击。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0550_000_0
#. timeline 1657..2424
#: codec/1/177/0xb1290/1
msgid ""
"Amanda's crew calls them \"scouts.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"阿曼达的人管他们叫“侦察兵”。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0550_000_0
#. timeline 2479..3510
#: codec/1/177/0xb1290/2
msgid ""
"They'll blend themselves in with the terrain and the\n"
"vegetation.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们会把自己与地形和\n"
"植被融为一体。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0550_000_0
#. timeline 3538..4263
#: codec/1/177/0xb1290/3
msgid ""
"Then, when they see you, they'll swoop in.\n"
msgstr ""
"然后一看到你，就扑上来。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0550_000_0
#. timeline 4318..4876
#: codec/1/177/0xb1290/4
msgid ""
"They fight pretty much like commandos\n"
msgstr ""
"他们打法跟特种兵差不多\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0550_000_0
#. timeline 4876..5670
#: codec/1/177/0xb1290/5
msgid ""
"and will use clearing techniques to flush you out.\n"
msgstr ""
"会用清场战术把你逼出来。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0550_000_0
#. timeline 5726..7049
#: codec/1/177/0xb1290/6
msgid ""
"In addition to wielding normal weapons, the scouts\n"
"also carry wires.\n"
msgstr ""
"侦察兵除了普通武器，\n"
"还带着钢丝。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0550_000_0
#. timeline 7077..8178
#: codec/1/177/0xb1290/7
msgid ""
"Hm... Sounds like these guys know their CQC.\n"
msgstr ""
"嗯……看来这帮人懂CQC。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0550_000_0
#. timeline 8192..9640
#: codec/1/177/0xb1290/8
msgid ""
"Could be. We've been getting reports of CQC\n"
"attacks being blocked by wires.\n"
msgstr ""
"有可能。我们收到报告说\n"
"CQC攻击被钢丝挡住了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0550_000_0
#. timeline 9668..10031
#: codec/1/177/0xb1290/9
msgid ""
"Stay alert.\n"
msgstr ""
"警惕。\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/0
msgid ""
"Scouts are outfitted with camouflage to help them\n"
"hide.\n"
msgstr ""
"侦察兵配有迷彩，\n"
"方便隐蔽。\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/1
msgid ""
"Some of them look kind of weird, like they've got\n"
"seaweed growing all over them.\n"
msgstr ""
"有些看着挺怪，\n"
"像长了一身海藻。\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/2
msgid ""
"Ah, ghillie suits.\n"
msgstr ""
"啊，吉利服。\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/3
msgid ""
"Not much difference between them and any other\n"
"scout in terms of combat ability,\n"
msgstr ""
"战斗力跟其他侦察兵\n"
"没多大差别，\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/4
msgid ""
"but it does make them harder to spot.\n"
msgstr ""
"但确实更难发现。\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/5
msgid ""
"I'm sure it does.\n"
msgstr ""
"那肯定。\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/6
msgid ""
"You've come across these before?\n"
msgstr ""
"你以前遇到过？\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/7
msgid ""
"Yeah. The Soviet Union...\n"
msgstr ""
"嗯。苏联……\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/8
msgid ""
"The first time, it took me a full hour to find the\n"
"guy and take him out...\n"
msgstr ""
"第一次我花了整整一小时\n"
"才找到他干掉……\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/9
msgid ""
"Kaz, do you know if they shine?\n"
msgstr ""
"卡兹，他们会发光吗？\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/10
msgid ""
"...Shine. Like how?\n"
msgstr ""
"……发光。怎么发？\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/11
msgid ""
"Like from their heads.\n"
msgstr ""
"从头上。\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/12
msgid ""
"Their heads?\n"
msgstr ""
"头上？\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/13
msgid ""
"How about their hair? Do they have a lot of it?\n"
msgstr ""
"头发呢？多不多？\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/14
msgid ""
"What are you talking about? How the hell would I\n"
"know?\n"
msgstr ""
"你在说什么？我他妈怎么\n"
"会知道？\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/15
msgid ""
"How about a parrot? Did anybody hear a parrot\n"
"squawk?\n"
msgstr ""
"鹦鹉怎么样？有人听到鹦鹉\n"
"叫吗？\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/16
msgid ""
"A parrot? Look, Snake, you're talking to the wrong\n"
"guy.\n"
msgstr ""
"鹦鹉？听着，Snake，你找错\n"
"人了。\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/17
msgid ""
"I mean, Cecile's the bird expert...\n"
msgstr ""
"塞西尔才是鸟类专家……\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/18
msgid ""
"Wait a second, what am I saying? You're not\n"
"making any sense to begin with!\n"
msgstr ""
"等等，我在说什么？\n"
"你本来就说得没头没脑！\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/19
msgid ""
"Never mind. It's... a long story. I'll figure out another\n"
"way. Forget about it.\n"
msgstr ""
"算了。这事……说来话长。我再想别的\n"
"办法吧。别管了。\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/20
msgid ""
"Yeah, I'll do that.\n"
msgstr ""
"好，就这么办。\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/21
msgid ""
"Anyway, we've already lost too many good people\n"
"to these surprise encounters.\n"
msgstr ""
"总之，这些遭遇战已经让我们损失了太多\n"
"好手。\n"

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/22
msgid ""
"Make sure you don't end up like one of them.\n"
msgstr ""
"别让自己也变成其中之一。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0570_000_0
#. timeline 445..1128
#: codec/1/177/0xb1db0/0
msgid ""
"There are areas out there where enemy soldiers\n"
"are\n"
msgstr ""
"有些区域里，敌人士兵\n"
"会\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0570_000_0
#. timeline 1128..2048
#: codec/1/177/0xb1db0/1
msgid ""
"deployed in multiple layers for extra coverage.\n"
msgstr ""
"多层布防，覆盖更严密。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0570_000_0
#. timeline 2075..2995
#: codec/1/177/0xb1db0/2
msgid ""
"More than a few of those will be attacking you\n"
"from a distance\n"
msgstr ""
"其中不少人会从远处\n"
"向你发起攻击\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0570_000_0
#. timeline 2995..3705
#: codec/1/177/0xb1db0/3
msgid ""
"- rooftops and far-off vantage points.\n"
msgstr ""
"——屋顶和远处的制高点。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0570_000_0
#. timeline 3733..4611
#: codec/1/177/0xb1db0/4
msgid ""
"Try not to get too distracted by nearby enemies,\n"
msgstr ""
"别被近处的敌人分散太多注意，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0570_000_0
#. timeline 4611..5823
#: codec/1/177/0xb1db0/5
msgid ""
"because you could be leaving yourself wide open\n"
"to longer-range attacks.\n"
msgstr ""
"因为那样你会完全暴露在\n"
"更远距离的攻击下。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0570_000_0
#. timeline 5823..6269
#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 7356..7787
#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0140_000_0
#. timeline 5517..5921
#: codec/1/177/0xb1db0/6
#: codec/1/186/0xbab50/8
#: codec/1/205/0xcd600/5
msgid ""
"I'll be careful.\n"
msgstr ""
"我会小心。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0580_000_0
#. timeline 445..1030
#: codec/1/178/0xb2060/0
msgid ""
"Enemy tanks, armored vehicles,\n"
msgstr ""
"敌方坦克、装甲车\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0580_000_0
#. timeline 1030..2173
#: codec/1/178/0xb2060/1
msgid ""
"and attack choppers are always accompanied by a\n"
"combat squad.\n"
msgstr ""
"而攻击直升机身边总跟着一支\n"
"战斗小队。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0580_000_0
#. timeline 2229..3051
#: codec/1/178/0xb2060/2
msgid ""
"The soldiers aren't particularly tough on their own.\n"
msgstr ""
"那些士兵单打独斗并不算强。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0580_000_0
#. timeline 3078..4263
#: codec/1/178/0xb2060/3
msgid ""
"What makes them formidable is how well they work\n"
"together as a team.\n"
msgstr ""
"它们难对付，就在于配合得\n"
"像一支队伍般默契。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0580_000_0
#. timeline 4291..5126
#: codec/1/178/0xb2060/4
msgid ""
"As if you didn't have enough to worry about with\n"
"the machine.\n"
msgstr ""
"好像光应付那台机器还不够你\n"
"操心似的。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0580_000_0
#. timeline 5140..5795
#: codec/1/178/0xb2060/5
msgid ""
"Good. I like a challenge.\n"
msgstr ""
"好。我喜欢挑战。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0580_000_0
#. timeline 5809..7035
#: codec/1/178/0xb2060/6
msgid ""
"Yeah, well, see how you feel when you actually\n"
"have to face them in battle.\n"
msgstr ""
"是啊，等你真在战斗中\n"
"面对它们，再看是什么感觉吧。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0580_000_0
#. timeline 7091..8052
#: codec/1/178/0xb2060/7
msgid ""
"Snake, whatever you do, don't let them surround\n"
"you.\n"
msgstr ""
"Snake，千万别让它们把你\n"
"包围了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0580_000_0
#. timeline 8066..9097
#: codec/1/178/0xb2060/8
msgid ""
"The last thing you need is to get pushed into the\n"
"vehicle's kill zone.\n"
msgstr ""
"你最不想遇到的就是被逼进\n"
"载具的杀伤区。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0580_000_0
#. timeline 9153..10086
#: codec/1/178/0xb2060/9
msgid ""
"And pay attention to what your enemies say to\n"
"each other.\n"
msgstr ""
"还要注意听敌人彼此之间\n"
"在说什么。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0580_000_0
#. timeline 10114..11201
#: codec/1/178/0xb2060/10
msgid ""
"You can improve your chances by figuring out\n"
"what they're planning\n"
msgstr ""
"弄清他们\n"
"在谋划什么，能提高你的胜算\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0580_000_0
#. timeline 11215..11939
#: codec/1/178/0xb2060/11
msgid ""
"and using it to preempt their movements.\n"
msgstr ""
"并借此抢先行动。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0580_000_0
#. timeline 11967..12845
#: codec/1/178/0xb2060/12
msgid ""
"You don't always have to go toe to toe to win a\n"
"fight.\n"
msgstr ""
"要赢一场战斗，并不非得\n"
"正面硬拼。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0580_000_0
#. timeline 12873..13500
#: codec/1/178/0xb2060/13
msgid ""
"Think like a guerrilla.\n"
msgstr ""
"像游击队员那样思考。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0590_000_0
#. timeline 459..1476
#: codec/1/178/0xb25a0/0
msgid ""
"Enemies carrying shields can be a real pain in the\n"
"ass.\n"
msgstr ""
"携带盾牌的敌人真是让人头疼得\n"
"要命。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0590_000_0
#. timeline 1532..2424
#: codec/1/178/0xb25a0/1
msgid ""
"To hear Amanda tell it, trying to fight those\n"
"bastards\n"
msgstr ""
"听阿曼达说，想跟那些\n"
"混蛋交手\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0590_000_0
#. timeline 2424..3371
#: codec/1/178/0xb25a0/2
msgid ""
"while they sit behind their shields taking pistol\n"
"shots at you\n"
msgstr ""
"他们却躲在盾牌后面朝你\n"
"开枪\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0590_000_0
#. timeline 3385..4109
#: codec/1/178/0xb25a0/3
msgid ""
"is enough to make you want to rip your hair out.\n"
msgstr ""
"能把你气得抓狂。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0590_000_0
#. timeline 4165..4778
#: codec/1/178/0xb25a0/4
msgid ""
"Get around and flank them if you can.\n"
msgstr ""
"能绕就绕到侧面包抄。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0590_000_0
#. timeline 4820..5976
#: codec/1/178/0xb25a0/5
msgid ""
"You might want to try blinding them with smoke or\n"
"stun grenades first.\n"
msgstr ""
"你可先用烟雾弹或\n"
"眩晕手雷让他们失明。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0590_000_0
#. timeline 6046..7509
#: codec/1/178/0xb25a0/6
msgid ""
"Also, armor-piercing rounds should make it a little\n"
"easier to punch through their shields.\n"
msgstr ""
"另外，穿甲弹应该能让你更容易\n"
"击穿他们的盾牌。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0590_000_0
#. timeline 7551..8066
#: codec/1/178/0xb25a0/7
msgid ""
"Use 'em if you've got 'em.\n"
msgstr ""
"有就用。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0640_000_0
#. timeline 459..1769
#: codec/1/178/0xb28e0/0
msgid ""
"We know there are variations in the kinds of gear\n"
"patrolmen and commandos wear,\n"
msgstr ""
"我们知道巡逻兵和突击队员穿戴的装备\n"
"种类存在差异，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0640_000_0
#. timeline 1769..2284
#: codec/1/178/0xb28e0/1
msgid ""
"especially the body armor.\n"
msgstr ""
"尤其是护甲。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0640_000_0
#. timeline 2326..3510
#: codec/1/178/0xb28e0/2
msgid ""
"Our scouts report that an enemy's defense and\n"
"firing accuracy\n"
msgstr ""
"侦察兵报告，敌人的防御和\n"
"射击精准度\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0640_000_0
#. timeline 3510..4472
#: codec/1/178/0xb28e0/3
msgid ""
"are directly proportional to how heavy their gear is.\n"
msgstr ""
"与装备重量成正比。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0640_000_0
#. timeline 4750..5628
#: codec/1/178/0xb28e0/4
msgid ""
"Those must be the guys with the highest combat\n"
"skills.\n"
msgstr ""
"那些人肯定就是战斗\n"
"技能最高的家伙。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0640_000_0
#. timeline 5656..6659
#: codec/1/178/0xb28e0/5
msgid ""
"They can fight in heavier gear without their\n"
"performance suffering.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们能穿着更重的装备作战，而\n"
"表现不会下降。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0640_000_0
#. timeline 6673..7857
#: codec/1/178/0xb28e0/6
msgid ""
"Supposedly it's pretty easy to tell the difference in\n"
"gear just by looking.\n"
msgstr ""
"据说光靠看就能很容易分辨出\n"
"装备的差异。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0640_000_0
#. timeline 7927..8233
#: codec/1/178/0xb28e0/7
msgid ""
"So remember:\n"
msgstr ""
"记住：\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0640_000_0
#. timeline 8233..9334
#: codec/1/178/0xb28e0/8
msgid ""
"use extra caution when dealing with enemies\n"
"wearing heavy gear.\n"
msgstr ""
"对付穿着重型装备的敌人时\n"
"要格外小心。\n"

#: codec/1/178/0xb2c50/0
msgid ""
"Enemies will try to fight you from different\n"
"distances\n"
msgstr ""
"敌人会尝试从不同的\n"
"距离与你交战\n"

#: codec/1/178/0xb2c50/1
msgid ""
"based on the weapon they've got equipped.\n"
msgstr ""
"在不同距离与你交战。\n"

#: codec/1/178/0xb2c50/2
msgid ""
"When you meet an enemy, get a good look at what\n"
"they're carrying\n"
msgstr ""
"遇到敌人时，仔细看清他们\n"
"拿着什么\n"

#: codec/1/178/0xb2c50/3
msgid ""
"- it can make or break your chances in battle.\n"
msgstr ""
"——这能决定战斗成败。\n"

#: codec/1/178/0xb2e10/0
msgid ""
"Enemies carrying handguns and shotguns will try\n"
"and get in close.\n"
msgstr ""
"携带手枪和霰弹枪的敌人会试图\n"
"靠近你。\n"

#: codec/1/178/0xb2e10/1
msgid ""
"That makes them dangerous, but at the same time\n"
"easier to hit.\n"
msgstr ""
"这让他们很危险，但同时也\n"
"更容易被击中。\n"

#: codec/1/178/0xb2e10/2
msgid ""
"Keep you wits about you and you can turn a threat\n"
"into an opportunity.\n"
msgstr ""
"保持头脑清醒，你就能把威胁\n"
"变成机会。\n"

#: codec/1/178/0xb2fa0/0
msgid ""
"Enemies carrying assault rifles and machine guns\n"
msgstr ""
"拿着突击步枪和机枪的敌人\n"

#: codec/1/178/0xb2fa0/1
msgid ""
"will usually fire at you from farther away.\n"
msgstr ""
"通常会在更远处向你开火。\n"

#: codec/1/178/0xb2fa0/2
msgid ""
"Use whatever cover you can find,\n"
msgstr ""
"利用能找到的一切掩体，\n"

#: codec/1/178/0xb2fa0/3
msgid ""
"then return fire with a few well-placed shots of\n"
"your own.\n"
msgstr ""
"再用几发精准的射击\n"
"还击。\n"

#: codec/1/179/0xb3140/0
msgid ""
"Don't expect enemies carrying sniper rifles\n"
msgstr ""
"别指望拿狙击枪的敌人\n"

#: codec/1/179/0xb3140/1
msgid ""
"or rocket launchers to get up close and personal.\n"
msgstr ""
"或者用火箭筒近身招呼。\n"

#: codec/1/179/0xb3140/2
msgid ""
"They'll be constantly moving from place to place\n"
msgstr ""
"他们会不停转移位置\n"

#: codec/1/179/0xb3140/3
msgid ""
"looking for an opening to snipe at you. Tricky\n"
"bastards.\n"
msgstr ""
"找机会狙击你。狡猾的\n"
"家伙。\n"

#: codec/1/179/0xb3140/4
msgid ""
"Eye for an eye, tooth for a tooth, - go with the\n"
"sniper rifle.\n"
msgstr ""
"以眼还眼，以牙还牙，- 用\n"
"狙击步枪上。\n"

#: codec/1/179/0xb3140/5
msgid ""
"Make sure you stay out of their line of sight,\n"
msgstr ""
"务必别进入他们视线，\n"

#: codec/1/179/0xb3140/6
msgid ""
"and when they expose themselves, take 'em down!\n"
msgstr ""
"等他们露头，就干掉！\n"

#: codec/1/179/0xb33f0/0
#: codec/1/179/0xb3490/0
#: codec/1/179/0xb3530/0
#: codec/1/179/0xb35d0/0
#: codec/1/179/0xb3670/0
msgid ""
"(dummy. not used)\n"
msgstr ""
"（占位）\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0010_000_0
#. timeline 473..1226
#: codec/1/179/0xb3710/0
msgid ""
"Costa Rica means \"rich coast\" in Spanish.\n"
msgstr ""
"哥斯达黎加在西班牙语里意为\"富饶海岸\"。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0010_000_0
#. timeline 1267..2089
#: codec/1/179/0xb3710/1
msgid ""
"Is it true that Columbus was the one who came up\n"
"with the name?\n"
msgstr ""
"真是哥伦布起的\n"
"名字吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0010_000_0
#. timeline 2173..3092
#: codec/1/179/0xb3710/2
msgid ""
"Your guess is as good as mine. But it is true\n"
msgstr ""
"我也说不准。但确实\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0010_000_0
#. timeline 3092..4388
#: codec/1/179/0xb3710/3
msgid ""
"that Columbus landed his ships near Limón back in\n"
"the Age of Exploration.\n"
msgstr ""
"当年哥伦布在大航海时代\n"
"把他的船停靠在利蒙附近。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0010_000_0
#. timeline 4458..5154
#: codec/1/179/0xb3710/4
msgid ""
"He wrote in his diary that when he landed,\n"
msgstr ""
"他在日记里写道，登陆时\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0010_000_0
#. timeline 5224..6352
#: codec/1/179/0xb3710/5
msgid ""
"the indígena showered him with gifts of gold.\n"
"Hence the name.\n"
msgstr ""
"原住民献给他大量黄金作礼。\n"
"因此得名。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0010_000_0
#. timeline 6394..6938
#: codec/1/179/0xb3710/6
msgid ""
"It sounds a little strange to me.\n"
msgstr ""
"我觉得有点奇怪。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0010_000_0
#. timeline 7007..7955
#: codec/1/179/0xb3710/7
msgid ""
"There is no way they could find that much gold in\n"
"Costa Rica.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们不可能在\n"
"哥斯达黎加找到那么多黄金。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0010_000_0
#. timeline 7983..9153
#: codec/1/179/0xb3710/8
msgid ""
"Columbus originally set sail in search of the\n"
"legendary land of gold.\n"
msgstr ""
"哥伦布最初出海是为了寻找\n"
"传说中的黄金之地。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0010_000_0
#. timeline 9320..9961
#: codec/1/179/0xb3710/9
msgid ""
"Maybe he was just nuts about the stuff.\n"
msgstr ""
"也许他就是痴迷那玩意儿。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0010_000_0
#. timeline 9975..10644
#: codec/1/179/0xb3710/10
msgid ""
"Costa Rica is rich enough without it.\n"
msgstr ""
"没黄金也够富饶。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0010_000_0
#. timeline 10727..11800
#: codec/1/179/0xb3710/11
msgid ""
"Look at the forests and the animals, and the\n"
"peace-loving people...\n"
msgstr ""
"看看森林、动物，还有\n"
"热爱和平的人民……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0010_000_0
#. timeline 11814..12329
#: codec/1/179/0xb3710/12
msgid ""
"That is what I want to protect.\n"
msgstr ""
"那才是我要保护的。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0010_000_0
#. timeline 12357..12914
#: codec/1/179/0xb3710/13
msgid ""
"...I know how you feel.\n"
msgstr ""
"……我懂你。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0020_000_0
#. timeline 473..1825
#: codec/1/179/0xb3be0/0
msgid ""
"Democracy took root in Costa Rica before\n"
"anywhere else in Central America.\n"
msgstr ""
"民主在哥斯达黎加扎根，\n"
"比中美洲任何地方都早。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0020_000_0
#. timeline 1894..3162
#: codec/1/179/0xb3be0/1
msgid ""
"Sure, we had coups and dictators and all, but\n"
"never a total meltdown.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们也有过政变和独裁，但\n"
"从未彻底崩溃。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0020_000_0
#. timeline 3287..4026
#: codec/1/179/0xb3be0/2
msgid ""
"That is, until 26 years ago...\n"
msgstr ""
"直到26年前……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0020_000_0
#. timeline 4082..5726
#: codec/1/179/0xb3be0/3
msgid ""
"The civil war. Yeah, I understand you lost your\n"
"grandparents.\n"
msgstr ""
"内战。是啊，我明白你失去了你的\n"
"祖父母。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0020_000_0
#. timeline 5753..6868
#: codec/1/179/0xb3be0/4
msgid ""
"It started with a dispute over alleged fraud in the\n"
"presidential election.\n"
msgstr ""
"起因是对总统选举中涉嫌舞弊的\n"
"争议。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0020_000_0
#. timeline 6993..8108
#: codec/1/179/0xb3be0/5
msgid ""
"What I don't understand is why friend turned\n"
"against friend\n"
msgstr ""
"我不明白的是，为什么朋友会\n"
"反目成仇\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0020_000_0
#. timeline 8192..8735
#: codec/1/179/0xb3be0/6
msgid ""
"when they could have talked it out instead.\n"
msgstr ""
"明明本可以谈开的。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0020_000_0
#. timeline 8832..9613
#: codec/1/179/0xb3be0/7
msgid ""
"Yeah, that... would have been nice.\n"
msgstr ""
"是啊，那样……就好了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0020_000_0
#. timeline 9682..10978
#: codec/1/179/0xb3be0/8
msgid ""
"Even today, some buildings still have bullet holes\n"
"from the civil war.\n"
msgstr ""
"即使在今天，一些建筑上仍留有内战时期的\n"
"弹孔。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0020_000_0
#. timeline 11089..12928
#: codec/1/179/0xb3be0/9
msgid ""
"A quarter century later, and it is a tragedy we\n"
"ticos cannot forget... Must not forget.\n"
msgstr ""
"二十五年过去，这是我们哥斯达黎加人\n"
"不能忘……绝不该忘的悲剧。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0020_000_0
#. timeline 13012..14294
#: codec/1/179/0xb3be0/10
msgid ""
"It was the year after the civil war that the army\n"
"was constitutionally abolished.\n"
msgstr ""
"内战结束后的那一年，军队\n"
"被依宪法废除。\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb4050/0
msgid ""
"A new president was elected this year - President\n"
"Oduber.\n"
msgstr ""
"今年选出了新总统——\n"
"奥杜贝尔总统。\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb4050/1
msgid ""
"He seems to be distancing himself from the United\n"
"States.\n"
msgstr ""
"他似乎正在与美国\n"
"保持距离。\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb4050/2
msgid ""
"He's limited the privileges granted to American\n"
"banks, lifted the sanctions on Cuba...\n"
msgstr ""
"他限制了给予美国银行的\n"
"特权，解除了对古巴的制裁……\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb4050/3
msgid ""
"Our last president was so pro-U.S., people\n"
"suspected he was in bed with the CIA.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们的上一任总统极其亲美，人们\n"
"怀疑他与中情局有染。\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb4050/4
msgid ""
"You think the CIA's doing this because it feels\n"
"threatened by the president's shift in policy...?\n"
msgstr ""
"你认为中情局这么做是因为它感到\n"
"受到总统政策转变的威胁……？\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb4050/5
msgid ""
"It is possible. But would they really bring in such a\n"
"huge army just because of that?\n"
msgstr ""
"有可能。但他们会仅仅因为这一点就出动\n"
"如此庞大的军队吗？\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb4050/6
msgid ""
"Part of our job is finding out.\n"
msgstr ""
"查明真相也是我们的工作之一。\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb4050/7
msgid ""
"Exactly. Thanks, Snake. Peace.\n"
msgstr ""
"没错。谢了，SNAKE。和平。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 487..1755
#: codec/1/180/0xb43c0/0
msgid ""
"So are you a student at the University for Peace,\n"
"Paz?\n"
msgstr ""
"那么，你是和平大学的学生吗，\n"
"帕兹？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 1797..2410
#: codec/1/180/0xb43c0/1
msgid ""
"No, I am still in high school.\n"
msgstr ""
"不，我还在上高中。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 2479..3761
#: codec/1/180/0xb43c0/2
msgid ""
"But Professor Gálvez lets me visit his office and\n"
"study with him every now and then.\n"
msgstr ""
"但加尔维斯教授允许我时不时去他的办公室\n"
"和他一起学习。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 3817..5419
#: codec/1/180/0xb43c0/3
msgid ""
"International law, security, conflict resolution,\n"
"human rights...\n"
msgstr ""
"国际法、安全、冲突解决、\n"
"人权……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 5489..6729
#: codec/1/180/0xb43c0/4
msgid ""
"We study all these subjects and then use them to\n"
"build the foundations of peace.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们学习所有这些科目，然后用它们来\n"
"构建和平的基础。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 6798..8373
#: codec/1/180/0xb43c0/5
msgid ""
"Yeah, I get it... I'd just never heard the UN had a\n"
"University for Peace before.\n"
msgstr ""
"是啊，我明白……我只是从没听说联合国有一所\n"
"和平大学。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 8387..10685
#: codec/1/180/0xb43c0/6
msgid ""
"Oh, that. Well, to be precise, it is still being set up.\n"
"They have started conducting research, but\n"
msgstr ""
"哦，那个。准确说，它还在筹建中。\n"
"他们已开始研究，但\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 10741..11563
#: codec/1/180/0xb43c0/7
msgid ""
"the UN has not passed the necessary resolution\n"
"yet.\n"
msgstr ""
"联合国尚未通过必要的\n"
"决议。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 11633..12260
#: codec/1/180/0xb43c0/8
msgid ""
"Professor Gálvez couldn't wait that long...\n"
msgstr ""
"加尔维斯教授等不了那么久……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 12274..12928
#: codec/1/180/0xb43c0/9
msgid ""
"Oh, uh, right.\n"
msgstr ""
"哦，对。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 12942..13514
#: codec/1/180/0xb43c0/10
msgid ""
"Costa Rica abolished its army,\n"
msgstr ""
"哥斯达黎加废除了军队，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 13555..14586
#: codec/1/180/0xb43c0/11
msgid ""
"and has also hosted the Central American Court of\n"
"Justice.\n"
msgstr ""
"还曾承办过中美洲\n"
"法院。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 14614..15993
#: codec/1/180/0xb43c0/12
msgid ""
"It is the perfect place to build a university like\n"
"ours, don't you think?\n"
msgstr ""
"在这里建我们这样的大学再合适不过，\n"
"你不觉得吗？\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/0
msgid ""
"Professor Gálvez was a KGB spy...?\n"
msgstr ""
"加尔维斯教授是克格勃间谍……？\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/1
msgid ""
"I thought he helped me out of genuine concern for\n"
"Costa Rica's future...\n"
msgstr ""
"我还以为他是真心为哥斯达黎加的未来\n"
"才帮我的……\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/2
msgid ""
"You didn't know?\n"
msgstr ""
"你不知道？\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/3
msgid ""
"How could I?! Believe me, Snake.\n"
msgstr ""
"我怎么会知道？！相信我，SNAKE。\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/4
msgid ""
"He introduced himself as a peace researcher at\n"
"the university.\n"
msgstr ""
"他自我介绍说是大学里的\n"
"和平研究员。\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/5
msgid ""
"He had an office and credentials and everything...\n"
msgstr ""
"有办公室、证件，一应俱全……\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/6
msgid ""
"They're masters at creating cover personas. They\n"
"think of everything\n"
msgstr ""
"他们是伪造身份的高手。他们\n"
"考虑到了一切\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/7
msgid ""
"- ID papers, jobs, sometimes even families.\n"
msgstr ""
"ID、工作，有时连家人都有。\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/8
msgid ""
"Don't feel bad you didn't see through it.\n"
msgstr ""
"没看穿也别自责。\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/9
msgid ""
"But you did?\n"
msgstr ""
"那你看穿了？\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/10
msgid ""
"From the first time we met.\n"
msgstr ""
"初见就看穿了。\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/11
msgid ""
"I wish you'd told me...\n"
msgstr ""
"真希望你告诉过我……\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/12
msgid ""
"Sorry. I didn't know if it'd be right.\n"
msgstr ""
"抱歉。我不确定该不该说。\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/13
msgid ""
"You might have gotten mixed up in things you\n"
"shouldn't.\n"
msgstr ""
"你可能卷入了你\n"
"不该卷入的事情。\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/14
msgid ""
"That is impressive, though. Sizing him up him at a\n"
"single glance.\n"
msgstr ""
"不过那真厉害。一眼就\n"
"看穿了他。\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/15
msgid ""
"He reeked.\n"
msgstr ""
"他一身味儿。\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/16
msgid ""
"Reeked?\n"
msgstr ""
"味？\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/17
msgid ""
"He had this unmistakable air about him...\n"
msgstr ""
"他身上有股藏不住的气息……\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/18
msgid ""
"The air of someone who's been given a mission\n"
"and will see it through no matter what.\n"
msgstr ""
"那种被赋予使命、无论如何都要\n"
"完成的人的气质。\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/19
msgid ""
"Like me. I could just smell it.\n"
msgstr ""
"跟我一样。一闻就知。\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/20
msgid ""
"That is amazing, Snake!\n"
msgstr ""
"太厉害了，SNAKE！\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/21
msgid ""
"Nah, I'm just kidding. It was his prosthetic hand.\n"
msgstr ""
"哪有，开玩笑的。是他的假手。\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/22
msgid ""
"Why would a professor from a peace university\n"
"need a tool for assassination?\n"
msgstr ""
"和平大学的教授\n"
"要暗杀工具做什么？\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/23
msgid ""
"...\n"
msgstr ""
"……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0060_000_0
#. timeline 473..1337
#: codec/1/180/0xb4fe0/0
msgid ""
"That coffee you guys brought us is pretty damn\n"
"good.\n"
msgstr ""
"你们送来的咖啡\n"
"还真不错。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0060_000_0
#. timeline 1365..2396
#: codec/1/180/0xb4fe0/1
msgid ""
"Isn't it? Costa Rican coffee is the best.\n"
msgstr ""
"是吧？哥斯达黎加的咖啡最棒。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0060_000_0
#. timeline 2452..3524
#: codec/1/180/0xb4fe0/2
msgid ""
"The Central Basin has all the right conditions for\n"
"growing coffee.\n"
msgstr ""
"中央盆地的条件\n"
"非常适合种咖啡。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0060_000_0
#. timeline 3594..5085
#: codec/1/180/0xb4fe0/3
msgid ""
"It is high in elevation, with steady temperatures\n"
"and well-drained, volcanic soils.\n"
msgstr ""
"海拔高、气温稳定，\n"
"还有排水良好的火山土。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0060_000_0
#. timeline 5126..5809
#: codec/1/180/0xb4fe0/4
msgid ""
"The \"professor\" certainly seems attached to it.\n"
msgstr ""
"那位“教授”看来很中意它。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0060_000_0
#. timeline 5851..7648
#: codec/1/180/0xb4fe0/5
msgid ""
"The coffee we drank on the boat coming over was\n"
"awful. It put him in such a terrible mood.\n"
msgstr ""
"在船上喝的咖啡难喝极了，\n"
"害他心情糟透了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0060_000_0
#. timeline 7690..8554
#: codec/1/180/0xb4fe0/6
msgid ""
"How come I never hear about Costa Rican coffee,\n"
"then?\n"
msgstr ""
"那我怎么从没听说过\n"
"哥斯达黎加咖啡？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0060_000_0
#. timeline 8582..9905
#: codec/1/180/0xb4fe0/7
msgid ""
"Because it gets bought up by wholesalers and\n"
"mixed with beans from other countries...\n"
msgstr ""
"因为都被批发商收走，\n"
"和别国的豆子混在一起……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0060_000_0
#. timeline 10017..11521
#: codec/1/180/0xb4fe0/8
msgid ""
"It is really a shame. Such wonderful beans and\n"
"nobody knows they're from Costa Rica.\n"
msgstr ""
"实在可惜。这么好的豆子，\n"
"却没人知道它来自哥斯达黎加。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0060_000_0
#. timeline 11828..12496
#: codec/1/180/0xb4fe0/9
msgid ""
"They should launch an ad campaign or something.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们该搞个广告活动什么的。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0060_000_0
#. timeline 12524..14099
#: codec/1/180/0xb4fe0/10
msgid ""
"Right! I hope one day people will recognize Costa\n"
"Rican coffee for what it is.\n"
msgstr ""
"就是！希望有朝一日大家\n"
"能看清哥斯达黎加咖啡的价值。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0060_000_0
#. timeline 14127..14544
#: codec/1/180/0xb4fe0/11
msgid ""
"I'm with you there.\n"
msgstr ""
"这点我同意。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0070_000_1
#. timeline 473..1365
#: codec/1/181/0xb54b0/0
msgid ""
"Are there any large-scale ruins in Costa Rica, Paz?\n"
msgstr ""
"哥斯达黎加有大型遗迹吗，帕兹？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0070_000_1
#. timeline 1407..2410
#: codec/1/181/0xb54b0/1
msgid ""
"There's a place east of Cartago called Guayabo.\n"
msgstr ""
"卡塔戈东边有个地方叫瓜亚沃。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0070_000_1
#. timeline 2493..3232
#: codec/1/181/0xb54b0/2
msgid ""
"They have ruins there, but they're not especially\n"
"big.\n"
msgstr ""
"那里有遗迹，但不算\n"
"特别大。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0070_000_1
#. timeline 3650..4486
#: codec/1/181/0xb54b0/3
msgid ""
"Not the place I'm thinking of... Any others?\n"
msgstr ""
"不是我想的地方……还有别的？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0070_000_1
#. timeline 4527..5935
#: codec/1/181/0xb54b0/4
msgid ""
"Well, if you go a little way across the border into\n"
"Nicaragua,\n"
msgstr ""
"嗯，越过边境进入\n"
"尼加拉瓜不远，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0070_000_1
#. timeline 6004..8219
#: codec/1/181/0xb54b0/5
msgid ""
"there's a place called La Fortaleza de la\n"
"Inmaculada Concepción. That's the only famous one.\n"
msgstr ""
"有个地方叫拉福塔莱萨·德·拉\n"
"因玛库拉达·康塞普西翁。就它出名。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0070_000_1
#. timeline 8261..9195
#: codec/1/181/0xb54b0/6
msgid ""
"Then what were those ruins I saw from up on\n"
"Irazu...?\n"
msgstr ""
"那我在伊拉苏山上\n"
"看到的遗迹是……？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0070_000_1
#. timeline 9250..10783
#: codec/1/181/0xb54b0/7
msgid ""
"There are a lot of things we still do not know\n"
"about Costa Rica's ancient civilizations.\n"
msgstr ""
"关于哥斯达黎加的古代文明，\n"
"我们还有很多未知。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0070_000_1
#. timeline 10839..11730
#: codec/1/181/0xb54b0/8
msgid ""
"There are giant stone spheres throughout the\n"
"country.\n"
msgstr ""
"全国各地都有巨大的\n"
"石球。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0070_000_1
#. timeline 11814..12719
#: codec/1/181/0xb54b0/9
msgid ""
"What they were used for is still a mystery.\n"
msgstr ""
"用途至今是个谜。\n"

#: codec/1/181/0xb58a0/0
msgid ""
"Paz, you said Costa Rica has no army, right?\n"
msgstr ""
"帕兹，你说过哥斯达黎加没有军队吧？\n"

#: codec/1/181/0xb58a0/1
msgid ""
"Correct. Article 12 of the constitution declared\n"
msgstr ""
"没错。宪法第12条宣布\n"

#: codec/1/181/0xb58a0/2
msgid ""
"that the army as a permanent institution is\n"
"abolished.\n"
msgstr ""
"军队作为一个常设机构\n"
"被废除。\n"

#: codec/1/181/0xb58a0/3
msgid ""
"It does permit us to organize armed forces for\n"
"national defense\n"
msgstr ""
"它确实允许我们组织武装力量用于\n"
"国防\n"

#: codec/1/181/0xb58a0/4
msgid ""
"based on inter-American treaties.\n"
msgstr ""
"按美洲国家条约组建。\n"

#: codec/1/181/0xb58a0/5
msgid ""
"Only temporarily, then.\n"
msgstr ""
"那只是暂时的。\n"

#: codec/1/181/0xb58a0/6
msgid ""
"In effect, yes. But in the years since the\n"
"constitution took effect,\n"
msgstr ""
"实际上，是的。但自\n"
"宪法生效以来的这些年里，\n"

#: codec/1/181/0xb58a0/7
msgid ""
"Costa Rica has not once raised an army.\n"
msgstr ""
"哥斯达黎加从未组建军队。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0080_010_0
#. timeline 445..1699
#: codec/1/181/0xb5b70/0
msgid ""
"Paz. How does your country defend itself without\n"
"an army?\n"
msgstr ""
"帕兹，你们国家没有军队，\n"
"靠什么自卫？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0080_010_0
#. timeline 1741..2535
#: codec/1/181/0xb5b70/1
msgid ""
"Especially in a rough neighborhood like Central\n"
"America.\n"
msgstr ""
"尤其是在中美洲\n"
"这种不太平的地带。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0080_010_0
#. timeline 2535..3148
#: codec/1/181/0xb5b70/2
msgid ""
"With the right kind of diplomacy.\n"
msgstr ""
"靠正确的外交。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0080_010_0
#. timeline 3204..4430
#: codec/1/181/0xb5b70/3
msgid ""
"If we live up to our ideals and earn the respect of\n"
"other countries,\n"
msgstr ""
"只要坚守理想、\n"
"赢得他国尊重，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0080_010_0
#. timeline 4486..5280
#: codec/1/181/0xb5b70/4
msgid ""
"the international community will support us.\n"
msgstr ""
"国际社会就会支持我们。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0080_010_0
#. timeline 5280..6046
#: codec/1/181/0xb5b70/5
msgid ""
"The two times Nicaragua actually did invade,\n"
msgstr ""
"尼加拉瓜真正入侵过两次，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0080_010_0
#. timeline 6060..7286
#: codec/1/181/0xb5b70/6
msgid ""
"the conflict was resolved diplomatically under OAS\n"
"(Organization of American States) auspices.\n"
msgstr ""
"两次都在美洲国家组织（OAS）\n"
"斡旋下通过外交解决。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0080_010_0
#. timeline 7314..8010
#: codec/1/181/0xb5b70/7
msgid ""
"Doesn't that leave you depending on the U.S. after\n"
"all?\n"
msgstr ""
"到头来不还是\n"
"得依赖美国？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0080_010_0
#. timeline 8010..9041
#: codec/1/181/0xb5b70/8
msgid ""
"American influence is unmatched, it is true.\n"
msgstr ""
"美国的影响力确实无人能及。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0080_010_0
#. timeline 9055..10086
#: codec/1/181/0xb5b70/9
msgid ""
"San Jose was critical of American policy at the\n"
"time...\n"
msgstr ""
"圣何塞当时批评过\n"
"美国的政策……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0080_010_0
#. timeline 10142..11688
#: codec/1/181/0xb5b70/10
msgid ""
"But America supported us all the same. It was\n"
"because we practiced peaceful diplomacy...\n"
msgstr ""
"但美国照样支持了我们。\n"
"因为我们奉行和平外交……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0080_010_0
#. timeline 11828..12246
#: codec/1/181/0xb5b70/11
msgid ""
"That is what I like to think.\n"
msgstr ""
"我愿意这样想。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0080_010_0
#. timeline 12260..12970
#: codec/1/181/0xb5b70/12
msgid ""
"That's one way to approach it, sure.\n"
msgstr ""
"这确实是一种思路。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0080_010_0
#. timeline 13082..14182
#: codec/1/181/0xb5b70/13
msgid ""
"But there are countries out there who'll use force\n"
"no matter how bad it looks.\n"
msgstr ""
"可有的国家不管多难看，\n"
"照样会动武。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0080_010_0
#. timeline 14210..15687
#: codec/1/181/0xb5b70/14
msgid ""
"Maybe so... I know my way of thinking probably\n"
"looks naïve to you.\n"
msgstr ""
"也许吧……我知道我的想法\n"
"在你看来大概很天真。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0080_010_0
#. timeline 15701..16690
#: codec/1/181/0xb5b70/15
msgid ""
"But it's not like we expect peace without working\n"
"for it.\n"
msgstr ""
"但我们并不指望\n"
"不付出就能换来和平。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0080_010_0
#. timeline 16746..17387
#: codec/1/181/0xb5b70/16
msgid ""
"Diplomacy is a battle in itself.\n"
msgstr ""
"外交本身就是一场战斗。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0080_010_0
#. timeline 17428..17777
#: codec/1/181/0xb5b70/17
msgid ""
"And we have to make the effort\n"
msgstr ""
"而且我们必须付出努力。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0080_010_0
#. timeline 17777..18640
#: codec/1/181/0xb5b70/18
msgid ""
"to seek out causes of misfortune and nip them in\n"
"the bud.\n"
msgstr ""
"找出不幸的根源，\n"
"在萌芽时掐掉。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0080_010_0
#. timeline 18849..19978
#: codec/1/181/0xb5b70/19
msgid ""
"It was that kind of thinking that got me trapped in\n"
"their base...\n"
msgstr ""
"正是这种想法，\n"
"让我被困在他们的基地……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0080_010_0
#. timeline 20647..21873
#: codec/1/181/0xb5b70/20
msgid ""
"I'm not blaming you. You haven't done anything\n"
"wrong.\n"
msgstr ""
"我没有怪你。\n"
"你没做错什么。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 473..1783
#: codec/1/182/0xb62e0/0
msgid ""
"The army was abolished 25 years ago, the year\n"
"after the civil war.\n"
msgstr ""
"军队在25年前被废除，也就是\n"
"内战后的第二年。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 1894..2869
#: codec/1/182/0xb62e0/1
msgid ""
"I learned about the sorrow of civil war from a very\n"
"young age.\n"
msgstr ""
"我从很小的时候\n"
"就了解到内战的悲伤。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 2995..4165
#: codec/1/182/0xb62e0/2
msgid ""
"The futility of countrymen fighting each other, and\n"
"the tragedy...\n"
msgstr ""
"同胞互相残杀的徒劳，以及\n"
"那场悲剧……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 4291..5377
#: codec/1/182/0xb62e0/3
msgid ""
"Costa Rica learned the hard way. That is why it\n"
"abolished its army.\n"
msgstr ""
"哥斯达黎加吃了大亏。所以才\n"
"废除了军队。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 5489..6394
#: codec/1/182/0xb62e0/4
msgid ""
"It decided to pour its efforts into education\n"
"instead.\n"
msgstr ""
"它决定转而将努力投入到\n"
"教育中。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 6548..7272
#: codec/1/182/0xb62e0/5
msgid ""
"\"More teachers than soldiers\" was the slogan.\n"
msgstr ""
"口号是“教师多于士兵”。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 7314..8080
#: codec/1/182/0xb62e0/6
msgid ""
"Education is essential, no question.\n"
msgstr ""
"教育必不可少。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 8247..9334
#: codec/1/182/0xb62e0/7
msgid ""
"Even Che used to teach reading and writing in\n"
"between guerrilla campaigns.\n"
msgstr ""
"就连切·格瓦拉也曾在\n"
"游击战间隙教人读书写字。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 9418..10644
#: codec/1/182/0xb62e0/8
msgid ""
"Costa Rica was poor at the time. We didn't have\n"
"many resources.\n"
msgstr ""
"当时哥斯达黎加很穷。我们\n"
"没有多少资源。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 10811..12246
#: codec/1/182/0xb62e0/9
msgid ""
"I suppose we had to pick one or the other - the\n"
"military or the schools.\n"
msgstr ""
"我想我们只能二选一——要么\n"
"军队，要么学校。\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb66e0/0
msgid ""
"Kaz was telling me Japan has a peace constitution,\n"
"too.\n"
msgstr ""
"卡兹告诉我，日本也有\n"
"一部和平宪法。\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb66e0/1
msgid ""
"That is right. Apparently when Costa Rica was\n"
"drafting its constitution,\n"
msgstr ""
"没错。据说哥斯达黎加在\n"
"起草宪法时，\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb66e0/2
msgid ""
"they looked to the Japanese as a model.\n"
msgstr ""
"就以日本为范本。\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb66e0/3
msgid ""
"Only Japan's constitution renounces war itself.\n"
msgstr ""
"只是日本宪法连战争权都放弃了。\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb66e0/5
msgid ""
"But... Japan has a Self-Defense Force, right? That I\n"
"do not get.\n"
msgstr ""
"但……日本有自卫队，对吧？这我\n"
"就不懂了。\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb66e0/6
msgid ""
"I think I will ask Mr. Miller about it next time I see\n"
"him. He said he used to be in the JSDF.\n"
msgstr ""
"我想下次见到米勒先生时问问他。\n"
"他说他以前在自卫队待过。\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb66e0/7
msgid ""
"You're a curious one, aren't you? Don't study too\n"
"hard.\n"
msgstr ""
"你真好奇。别太\n"
"用功了。\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/0
msgid ""
"What was that you were saying... \"peace is not the\n"
"natural state of men\"?\n"
msgstr ""
"你刚才说什么来着……“和平并非\n"
"人类的天性”？\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/1
msgid ""
"You said you learned it in school.\n"
msgstr ""
"你说这是在学校学的。\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/2
msgid ""
"That's right. They're the words of the German\n"
"philosopher Immanuel Kant.\n"
msgstr ""
"没错。这是德国\n"
"哲学家伊曼努尔·康德的话。\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/3
msgid ""
"In 1795 he wrote a book titled \"Perpetual Peace.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"1795年他写了本书叫《永久和平》。\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/4
msgid ""
"Kant argued that it's precisely because peace is\n"
"unnatural\n"
msgstr ""
"康德认为，正因为和平是\n"
"非自然的，\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/5
msgid ""
"that we have to make it ourselves.\n"
msgstr ""
"才要靠我们自己去创造。\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/6
msgid ""
"How?\n"
msgstr ""
"怎么创造？\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/7
msgid ""
"That's what his book is about. Is the concept\n"
"starting to sound interesting now?\n"
msgstr ""
"他书里就讲这个。现在这理念\n"
"听着有意思了？\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/8
msgid ""
"Not really... I belong in a more natural world.\n"
msgstr ""
"还好……我更适合自然的世界。\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/9
msgid ""
"Is that so...\n"
msgstr ""
"是吗……\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/10
msgid ""
"...My grandparents died in the civil war.\n"
msgstr ""
"……我祖父母死于内战。\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/11
msgid ""
"If only we'd been at peace, they wouldn't have lost\n"
"their lives.\n"
msgstr ""
"要是我们身处和平，他们就不会\n"
"丧命了。\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/12
msgid ""
"You actually wish for war?\n"
msgstr ""
"你其实渴望战争？\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/13
msgid ""
"It's not like I want to hurt innocent civilians.\n"
msgstr ""
"我又不是想伤害无辜平民。\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/14
msgid ""
"But if someone attacks you, what are you\n"
"supposed to do?\n"
msgstr ""
"但如果有人攻击你，你\n"
"该怎么办？\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/15
msgid ""
"A country needs the strength to defend itself.\n"
msgstr ""
"国家必须有自卫的力量。\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/16
msgid ""
"Otherwise it faces invasion, oppression, political\n"
"subjugation.\n"
msgstr ""
"否则它就会面临侵略、压迫、政治\n"
"征服。\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/17
msgid ""
"If they'd simply stop using force to tangle with\n"
"each other,\n"
msgstr ""
"如果他们干脆停止使用武力来互相\n"
"纠缠，\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/18
msgid ""
"countries wouldn't need force to defend themselves.\n"
msgstr ""
"国家就不需要武力自卫。\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/19
msgid ""
"And how would you guarantee that?\n"
msgstr ""
"那你怎么保证？\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/20
msgid ""
"I...\n"
msgstr ""
"我……\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/21
msgid ""
"...Sorry. But you have to understand how the world\n"
"works\n"
msgstr ""
"……抱歉。但你得明白世界\n"
"怎么运转\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/22
msgid ""
"in order to protect the ones you love.\n"
msgstr ""
"才能保护你所爱的人。\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/23
msgid ""
"That's not to say ideals aren't important, too. They\n"
"are.\n"
msgstr ""
"这并不是说理想就不重要。它们\n"
"很重要。\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/24
msgid ""
"You are right, Snake... Thanks. Peace!\n"
msgstr ""
"你说得对，SNAKE……谢谢。和平！\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb71f0/0
msgid ""
"Costa Rica's forests are more diverse than you\n"
"might expect.\n"
msgstr ""
"哥斯达黎加的森林比你\n"
"想象的更加多样。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb71f0/1
msgid ""
"Not all of them are tropical rain forests.\n"
msgstr ""
"不全是热带雨林。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb71f0/2
msgid ""
"Costa Rica is close to the Equator, it is true, but it\n"
"is also very mountainous.\n"
msgstr ""
"哥斯达黎加确实靠近赤道，但它\n"
"也非常多山。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb71f0/3
msgid ""
"I see what you mean.\n"
msgstr ""
"我懂你意思。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb71f0/4
msgid ""
"Go up 4,000 feet in elevation and the temperature\n"
"drops more than seven degrees.\n"
msgstr ""
"海拔每升高4000英尺，气温\n"
"就会下降超过七度。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb71f0/5
msgid ""
"There are basically three types of forests.\n"
msgstr ""
"森林基本分三类。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb71f0/6
msgid ""
"The lowlands are covered in tropical rain forests,\n"
"the highlands by tropical cloud forests.\n"
msgstr ""
"低地覆盖着热带雨林，\n"
"高地则覆盖着热带云雾林。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb71f0/7
msgid ""
"And areas where there is a dry season have\n"
"tropical dry forests.\n"
msgstr ""
"而有旱季的地区则分布着\n"
"热带干燥森林。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0120_010_0
#. timeline 473..2034
#: codec/1/183/0xb7530/0
msgid ""
"The lowlands along the Caribbean coast are mostly\n"
"covered by hot, humid tropical rain forests.\n"
msgstr ""
"加勒比海岸沿线的低地大部分\n"
"覆盖着炎热潮湿的热带雨林。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0120_010_0
#. timeline 2131..2897
#: codec/1/183/0xb7530/1
msgid ""
"What most people envision when they think of\n"
"\"jungle.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"多数人想到\n"
"“丛林”时的画面。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0120_010_0
#. timeline 3009..4374
#: codec/1/183/0xb7530/2
msgid ""
"The closely packed trees spread their branches\n"
"out at great heights to soak up the sun.\n"
msgstr ""
"茂密拥挤的树木在高处\n"
"伸展枝叶，以吸收阳光。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0120_010_0
#. timeline 4527..5530
#: codec/1/183/0xb7530/3
msgid ""
"Their shade makes it dark near the ground, so be\n"
"careful.\n"
msgstr ""
"树荫让地面附近很暗，要\n"
"小心。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0120_010_0
#. timeline 5600..6757
#: codec/1/183/0xb7530/4
msgid ""
"Of course, with so little light few plants can grow\n"
"on the ground,\n"
msgstr ""
"当然，光太少，没几株植物能长在\n"
"地上，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0120_010_0
#. timeline 6812..7439
#: codec/1/183/0xb7530/5
msgid ""
"so it might actually be easier to walk.\n"
msgstr ""
"那走路可能反而更轻松。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0120_010_0
#. timeline 7481..8791
#: codec/1/183/0xb7530/6
msgid ""
"So even if you could photosynthesize, it wouldn't\n"
"do you any good.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以就算你能光合作用，也没\n"
"好处。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0120_010_0
#. timeline 8860..9738
#: codec/1/183/0xb7530/7
msgid ""
"Photosynthesize? People cannot do that.\n"
msgstr ""
"光合作用？人做不到。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0120_010_0
#. timeline 10128..10602
#: codec/1/183/0xb7530/8
msgid ""
"Most people, anyway.\n"
msgstr ""
"多数人不行。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb78c0/0
msgid ""
"Areas with a distinct dry season, like the Pacific\n"
"coast, have tropical dry forests.\n"
msgstr ""
"有明显旱季的地区，比如太平洋沿岸，\n"
"分布着热带干林。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb78c0/1
msgid ""
"During the dry season, the trees drop their leaves.\n"
"It gives you a clearer view,\n"
msgstr ""
"旱季时，树木会落叶。\n"
"这让你视野更清晰，\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb78c0/2
msgid ""
"but at the same time there are fewer places to\n"
"hide, so be careful.\n"
msgstr ""
"但同时也少了可以\n"
"躲藏的地方，所以要小心。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb78c0/3
msgid ""
"Sounds dull.\n"
msgstr ""
"听着挺无聊。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb78c0/4
msgid ""
"It is not, really. A lot of trees flower during the dry\n"
"season.\n"
msgstr ""
"其实并不是。很多树在旱季\n"
"开花。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb78c0/5
msgid ""
"Including my favorite, the tabebuia.\n"
msgstr ""
"包括我最喜欢的黄花风铃木。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb78c0/6
msgid ""
"It has these amazingly vivid yellow flowers.\n"
msgstr ""
"开着极其鲜艳的黄花。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb7b80/0
msgid ""
"The cloud forests cover the central mountainous\n"
"region of the country.\n"
msgstr ""
"云雾林覆盖着该国的中部\n"
"山区。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb7b80/1
msgid ""
"They're perpetually shrouded in fog. You get wet\n"
"just standing there.\n"
msgstr ""
"它们常年笼罩在雾中。你光是\n"
"站在那里就会湿透。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb7b80/2
msgid ""
"It is as if the entire forest is inside a cloud.\n"
msgstr ""
"仿佛整片森林都在云里。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb7b80/3
msgid ""
"Must make for poor visibility.\n"
msgstr ""
"那视野肯定很差。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb7b80/4
msgid ""
"It does. But beauty, too. It is like being lost in some\n"
"mystical, green labyrinth.\n"
msgstr ""
"确实。但也美。像迷失在某个\n"
"神秘绿色迷宫。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb7b80/5
msgid ""
"...I'd rather not get lost if that's OK.\n"
msgstr ""
"……可以的话，我不想迷路。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb7b80/6
msgid ""
"The forests are also home to lots of rare animals.\n"
msgstr ""
"森林里还栖息着许多珍稀动物。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb7b80/7
msgid ""
"Especially brightly colored frogs. They like the\n"
"humidity.\n"
msgstr ""
"尤其是色彩鲜艳的青蛙。它们喜欢\n"
"潮湿。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb7ea0/0
msgid ""
"You know that butterfly painted on Peace Walker -\n"
"any idea what that is?\n"
msgstr ""
"和平行者身上画的那只蝴蝶，\n"
"你知道是什么吗？\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb7ea0/1
msgid ""
"...It is a Morpho. A Peleides Morpho, if I'm not\n"
"mistaken.\n"
msgstr ""
"……是闪蝶。如果没记错，\n"
"是佩莱德斯闪蝶。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb7ea0/2
msgid ""
"Peleides Morpho?\n"
msgstr ""
"佩莱德斯闪蝶？\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb7ea0/3
msgid ""
"Uh huh. It is the most common type of Morpho in\n"
"Costa Rica.\n"
msgstr ""
"嗯。它是哥斯达黎加\n"
"最常见的闪蝶。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0160_010_0
#. timeline 5739..5935
#: codec/1/183/0xb7ea0/4
#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/4
#: codec/1/252/0xfc8d0/6
msgid ""
"Huh.\n"
msgstr ""
"哦。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb7ea0/5
msgid ""
"It has these gorgeous metallic blue wings that\n"
"shimmer in the light.\n"
msgstr ""
"它有一对漂亮的金属蓝翅膀，\n"
"在光下闪烁。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb7ea0/6
msgid ""
"You can see them even from a distance.\n"
msgstr ""
"隔着老远也看得见。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb7ea0/7
msgid ""
"You mean they reflect light?\n"
msgstr ""
"你是说它们反光？\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb7ea0/8
msgid ""
"Correct. It's called structural color. Morpho scales\n"
"have tiny bumps on them\n"
msgstr ""
"没错。这叫结构色。\n"
"闪蝶的鳞片上有微小的凸起，\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb7ea0/9
msgid ""
"that interfere with the light and make them look\n"
"blue.\n"
msgstr ""
"会和光发生干涉，\n"
"于是看起来是蓝色。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb7ea0/10
msgid ""
"The space between the bumps corresponds to the\n"
"wavelength of blue light...\n"
msgstr ""
"凸起间的间距，\n"
"正好对应蓝光的波长……\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb7ea0/11
msgid ""
"Let me see if I get this.\n"
msgstr ""
"我看看理解得对不对。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb7ea0/12
msgid ""
"So if you could change the spacing, you'd end up\n"
"seeing a different color?\n"
msgstr ""
"那么只要改变间距，\n"
"就会看到不同的颜色？\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb7ea0/13
msgid ""
"That's the principle.\n"
msgstr ""
"就是这个原理。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb7ea0/14
msgid ""
"I heard somewhere it's being researched as a way\n"
"to color cloth without dye.\n"
msgstr ""
"我听说有人在研究\n"
"用它做无染色的布料。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb7ea0/15
msgid ""
"Think of the camouflage you could make with that...\n"
msgstr ""
"想想能用它做出什么样的迷彩……\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb7ea0/16
msgid ""
"Is that all you can think of?\n"
msgstr ""
"你就只想到这个？\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb7ea0/17
msgid ""
"Hey, it's important. What I don't get is why they'd\n"
"put a butterfly on Peace Walker...\n"
msgstr ""
"嘿，这很重要。我不明白的是，\n"
"为什么要在和平行者上放蝴蝶……\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb7ea0/18
msgid ""
"Maybe because it looks pretty.\n"
msgstr ""
"也许只是因为好看。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb7ea0/19
msgid ""
"I hope that's all it is...\n"
msgstr ""
"希望只是这样……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 473..1825
#: codec/1/184/0xb8540/0
msgid ""
"Costa Rica is said to have about 87,000 species\n"
"of living things.\n"
msgstr ""
"据说哥斯达黎加约有87,000种\n"
"生物。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 1922..2925
#: codec/1/184/0xb8540/1
#, c-format
msgid ""
"That's about 5% of all the known species in the\n"
"world.\n"
msgstr ""
"这大约占世界上所有已知物种的\n"
"5%。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 2967..4235
#: codec/1/184/0xb8540/2
msgid ""
"A tiny place like this? I'll be damned.\n"
msgstr ""
"这么小的地方？真没想到。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 4263..5057
#: codec/1/184/0xb8540/3
msgid ""
"I want to protect that biological diversity.\n"
msgstr ""
"我想保护这种生物多样性。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 5154..6102
#: codec/1/184/0xb8540/4
msgid ""
"When diversity is lost, the environment weakens.\n"
msgstr ""
"多样性一失，环境就弱。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 6185..6729
#: codec/1/184/0xb8540/5
msgid ""
"Just look at the plantations.\n"
msgstr ""
"看看种植园吧。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 6784..8192
#: codec/1/184/0xb8540/6
msgid ""
"I think I know what you mean. It's like trying to\n"
"assemble a unit from similar guys\n"
msgstr ""
"我懂你的意思。就像用一群相似的人\n"
"组队\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 8331..8958
#: codec/1/184/0xb8540/7
msgid ""
"- it usually doesn't work out.\n"
msgstr ""
"往往行不通。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 8986..10017
#: codec/1/184/0xb8540/8
msgid ""
"Throw a few square pegs in there and everything\n"
"falls into place.\n"
msgstr ""
"掺几个格格不入的人进去，一切\n"
"就顺了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 10058..11243
#: codec/1/184/0xb8540/9
msgid ""
"There are so many species here that a lot of them\n"
"have not even been classified yet.\n"
msgstr ""
"这里物种太多了，很多\n"
"连分类都还没做。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 11312..12678
#: codec/1/184/0xb8540/10
msgid ""
"I'm hoping I can help do that someday. Kind of like\n"
"a parataxonomist.\n"
msgstr ""
"希望有朝一日我也能帮上忙。有点像\n"
"副分类学家。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 12692..13527
#: codec/1/184/0xb8540/11
msgid ""
"Para... say that again?\n"
msgstr ""
"副……再说？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 13555..14503
#: codec/1/184/0xb8540/12
msgid ""
"Parataxonomist. Someone who helps a taxonomist.\n"
msgstr ""
"副分类学家。协助分类学家的人。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 14517..16147
#: codec/1/184/0xb8540/13
msgid ""
"Oh. Huh. I thought you were going to say it had\n"
"something to do with parachutes.\n"
msgstr ""
"哦。哈。我还以为你要说\n"
"跟降落伞有关。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 16551..16913
#: codec/1/184/0xb8540/14
msgid ""
"You're weird...\n"
msgstr ""
"你真怪……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 473..2131
#: codec/1/184/0xb8a90/0
msgid ""
"The Development Corporation of Costa Rica, or\n"
"CODESA, was established two years ago.\n"
msgstr ""
"哥斯达黎加开发公司，简称\n"
"CODESA，两年前成立。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 2215..3023
#: codec/1/184/0xb8a90/1
msgid ""
"Since President Oduber was elected this year,\n"
msgstr ""
"今年奥杜贝尔总统当选后，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 3092..3914
#: codec/1/184/0xb8a90/2
msgid ""
"the state has been putting a lot more effort into\n"
"development.\n"
msgstr ""
"国家在开发上投入了更多\n"
"精力。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 4012..4736
#: codec/1/184/0xb8a90/3
msgid ""
"The corporate state, so to speak.\n"
msgstr ""
"可以说是公司化国家。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 4778..5767
#: codec/1/184/0xb8a90/4
msgid ""
"Growth is good and all, but there's one thing that\n"
"bugs me.\n"
msgstr ""
"发展是好事，但有件事让我\n"
"在意。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 5767..5976
#: codec/1/184/0xb8a90/5
#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/37
msgid ""
"What's that?\n"
msgstr ""
"什么事？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 6004..7258
#: codec/1/184/0xb8a90/6
msgid ""
"I cannot help but wonder whether CODESA is not\n"
"just a front for la CIA.\n"
msgstr ""
"我不禁怀疑CODESA是不是\n"
"CIA的幌子。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 7286..7843
#: codec/1/184/0xb8a90/7
msgid ""
"You mean what the \"professor\" was saying\n"
msgstr ""
"你是说那位“教授”说的\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 7843..8721
#: codec/1/184/0xb8a90/8
msgid ""
"about the CIA mercenaries posing as security\n"
"guards?\n"
msgstr ""
"CIA雇佣兵冒充保安\n"
"的事？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 8763..9404
#: codec/1/184/0xb8a90/9
msgid ""
"They were using CODESA as camouflage...\n"
msgstr ""
"他们拿CODESA当掩护……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 9431..10295
#: codec/1/184/0xb8a90/10
msgid ""
"I'm worried that development is going to destroy\n"
"the forests...\n"
msgstr ""
"我担心开发会毁掉\n"
"森林……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 10435..11257
#: codec/1/184/0xb8a90/11
msgid ""
"but I do not suppose it has anything to do with this.\n"
msgstr ""
"但我想这跟那事无关。\n"

#: codec/1/184/0xb8ee0/0
msgid ""
"My mother was the one who named me \"Paz.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"「帕兹」这名字是我母亲取的。\n"

#: codec/1/184/0xb8ee0/1
msgid ""
"She said it was an expression of her wish that the\n"
"country stay at peace.\n"
msgstr ""
"她说，这寄托了她希望\n"
"国家永享和平的心愿。\n"

#: codec/1/184/0xb8ee0/2
msgid ""
"It's a pretty common name in Central America.\n"
msgstr ""
"这名字在中美洲很常见。\n"

#: codec/1/184/0xb8ee0/3
msgid ""
"My mother always used to tell me, \"Never make\n"
"war. Always help keep the peace.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"母亲总对我说：\n"
"“永不发动战争。永远守护和平。”\n"

#: codec/1/184/0xb8ee0/4
msgid ""
"I remember... Your grandparents.\n"
msgstr ""
"我记得……你的祖父母。\n"

#: codec/1/184/0xb8ee0/5
msgid ""
"Yes, they died in the civil war. I think that is why\n"
"my mother hated war so much,\n"
msgstr ""
"是的，他们死于内战。\n"
"我想这就是母亲那么憎恨战争的原因，\n"

#: codec/1/184/0xb8ee0/6
msgid ""
"That's another thing you've got in common with\n"
"Kaz. His mother named him \"Peace,\" too.\n"
msgstr ""
"这也是你和卡兹的另一个共同点。\n"
"他母亲也给他取名叫“和平”。\n"

#: codec/1/184/0xb8ee0/7
msgid ""
"Si, because Japan also suffered through war. I\n"
"think I know how Mr. Miller's mother felt.\n"
msgstr ""
"是的，因为日本也饱受战争之苦。\n"
"我想我能体会米勒母亲的心情。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0040_000_0
#. timeline 473..975
#: codec/1/185/0xb9250/0
msgid ""
"You like the peace sign, huh?\n"
msgstr ""
"你喜欢和平手势啊？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0040_000_0
#. timeline 1003..2340
#: codec/1/185/0xb9250/1
msgid ""
"Sí. As a gesture it connects every peace-loving\n"
"person.\n"
msgstr ""
"是。这个手势连接着每个\n"
"爱好和平的人。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0040_000_0
#. timeline 2452..3441
#: codec/1/185/0xb9250/2
msgid ""
"Here, you try it, Snake. Peace!\n"
msgstr ""
"来，你试试，SNAKE。和平！\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0040_000_0
#. timeline 3496..4388
#: codec/1/185/0xb9250/3
msgid ""
"...No thanks. It... doesn't suit me.\n"
msgstr ""
"……不了。那……不适合我。\n"
